            0.306
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you explain how the mean is the centre of each collection?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.308,
            0.802,
            0.384
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Is the mean the midpoint of the two endpoints/extremes of the data? It is not always so. Instead, the total distances are equal on both the sides of the mean. This is illustrated through the following dot plots."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
